// A module meets a module trait's function by a recast's difference alone
// (module_trait_variance). What is refused: a parameter that asks for more than
// the trait gives (a '&mut P' for the trait's '&P'), a result that promises less
// (a '&P' for the trait's '&mut P'), a parameter or a result that needs a
// conversion (a wider number), a variant or an enum held by value for the other
// (not one layout, so a function reference refuses it too:
// ref_typecheck_fnref_byvalue), a value behind a '&mut' that differs at all, a
// parameter narrower than the trait's, a C-named function for a Cone one, and a
// name whose only candidates are two looser ones (neither is the one). Each is
// reported where the 'is' is written, naming the member.
//
// Type check stage. hosts.cone declares the trait, all defaults, and each
// one-file module beside it conforms to Runner declaring just the one it differs in:
//   asksmore.cone      read: a '&mut P' where the trait lends a '&P'
//   promisesless.cone  give: a '&P' where the trait returns a '&mut P'
//   widerparm.cone     count: an i64 parameter for the trait's i32
//   widerresult.cone   count: an i64 result for the trait's i32
//   byvalueparm.cone   hold: a Shape for the trait's Shape.Circle, by value
//   byvalueresult.cone lift: a Shape.Circle result for the trait's Shape
//   behindmut.cone     edit: a '&mut Shape.Circle' for the trait's '&mut Shape'
//   narrower.cone      size: a '&Shape.Circle' parameter for the trait's '&Shape'
//   cnamed.cone        count: a C-named function for the trait's Cone one
//   ambiguous.cone     inspect: two looser candidates and none of the trait's own

mod module_trait_typecheck_variance;
